<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simeto</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Symaethus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Simeto, the ancient Symaethus, is the river with the largest basin in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. It rises in the Nebrodi mountains, flows around the western and southern flanks of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-etna">Mount Etna</a>, and reaches the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-sea">Ionian Sea</a> south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catania">Catania</a>. Its plain, the Plain of Catania, is the largest in Sicily and has long been rich farmland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simeto.jpg" alt="Simeto" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Goribau · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simeto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
